+# N30 closed execution contract
+
+CPU preparation only. No artifact in this source grants release. The screen is 12 fresh original Dev identities in task-major C0/Q0/N30 order for tasks 0–3. C0 consumes baseline4; Q0 and N30 consume development8. There is no retry, continuation, inherited outcome, validation or formal route. Any reservation prevents automatic restart. A complete triple is the only early numerical stopping boundary: N30 successes plus remaining tasks below3. Promotion requires all12 valid, N30 >=3/4 and >=both controls, substantive guided QD/ED and at least one verified continuation insertion. An inserted row need not be selected. Costs, unrun outcomes and unknown tokens retain their actual denominators; missing is never zero.
+
+## Science and evidence
+
+The normal N30 profile is the accepted Q0 profile plus executed_progress_continuation_mode=executed_progress_continuation_v1. The previous actual winner is stored in native dtype before its FP32 decoder representation. All8 committed commands and actual EEF acknowledgments must align; index starts at1. Progress compares original Main target/EEF snapshots as CPU float64 against the previous fixed target. A valid immediate next guided identity inserts the previous native suffix56 and fresh row15 tail8; the other15 rows remain fresh. The unchanged mask is shape(1,1,128), model/native dtype, ones only at [10,39,40,41,42,43,44]. Decode uses the real converter: gripper raw<0 becomes-1, otherwise+1 including zero. No provider/model/score/RNG call is added.
+
+The only Phase B scientific-adjacent changes beyond accepted9029 are the approved passive Main packet event and the future QD-removal config consistency flag. Main records n30_observation_context after begin_decision and before policy invocation from the existing packet; no observation query. The independent audit binds this to policy double snapshots and, for step>0 without terminal reset, original dtype/bytes of the previous pre_reset_outcome EEF. It does not substitute controller.ee_pos. Legal unguided None keypoints/tracker must agree with the generic context and clear history. Ordinary inactive semantics are separate from malformed evidence.
+
+The independent source recognizer parses the complete frozen provider template and compiles, but never executes, its source with the original exec-string filename '<string>' to reconstruct canonical code_structure_sha256. It does not treat a valid hex string as proof or use unstable marshal reference/interning markers as cross-chunk identity. It does not call the online ProgressContinuation eligibility/copy function.
+
+Generic native audit plus N30 replay occur inside the same owned metered worker, after unchanged main.py. C0/Q0/N30 use CPU arithmetic audit; they do not enter the N23–N29 CUDA-arithmetic family. All arms require the N30-family profile gate even if guided=0. Missing eds_metrics is legal only when compute/generic canonical evidence establishes zero guided work. The receipt binds source, main argv, attempt, PID/start ticks/boot, report, indexed evidence hashes and optional-metrics presence. Supervisors verify hashes/JSON/scalars, never rerun tensors or CUDA. Verification of receipt evidence hashes can reread native files as bytes; it is not another arithmetic replay. Whole-worker wall time includes main, provider waits, audit and exit.
+
+Actual Q0-matched total guided costs remain21 model forwards×16 rows,19 RBF calls×16 rows,16 score batches/256 reward evaluations; primary canonical costs are11/176. Unguided retains5 forwards×1 row. Active-only initial_final diagnostic association reuses the actual composed canonical score and passively retains fresh native population; it adds no scoring. Costs differ across episodes when guidance differs.
+
+Future executed_progress_continuation_control=qd_off_v1 is CPU-only compatibility preparation: archive none/parent uniform_cells, same continuation/ED/feedback, no actual QD archive or archive allocation decisions. Normal mode requires grid_archive/sparse_priority. Current candidate profiles, plan and worker reject qd_off_v1; a future formal control requires a separate protocol/release. No extra Dev arm is authorized.
+
+## Shallow source and history bridge
+
+The new source record has exactly worker.source_record schema: commit, sorted files[{path,sha256}], canonical file-list sha256. Include all411 d855 files plus every new N30 source/profile/test/document and pinned Phase A JSON. reverse-source-v1.json restores six changed existing d855 files byte-exactly; all other405 remain unchanged. The separate Phase A reverse record restores only the approved post9029 main/policy/helper/config deltas and certifies all other Phase A source bytes unchanged.
+
+The bridge reads only the four hash-bound N29 JSON metadata records in historical-input-bindings-v1.json: accepted terminal review, final source/runtime review, frozen original40-row Dev plan, existing finite budget authority. Each is bounded at2MiB. Runtime is separately checked by normal admission. There is no recursive old-controller/proof execution or historic tensor replay. The old accepted root review attests old validity/proofs; it does not certify new N30 operations. No N30 standalone tensor preflight exists.
+
+## Admission and budgets
+
+Root retains existing578/100 cumulative caps, buckets76/262/180/40/20, validation32/formal12 protected GPUh and n29_budget_authority. Root adds n30_dev_authority only after source/runtime review. N30 local6h includes all N30 attempt/wait/audit/failure costs and any explicitly metered preparation. No preparation is launched here. Attempt capacity for remaining baseline4/development8 and protected attempts is checked before freeze/launch. Every episode must reserve full1800+40s against both local and cumulative unprotected hours before reservation. ResourceBudgetIncomplete closes as RESOURCE_BUDGET_INCOMPLETE, not a scientific failure. Inconsistent cost/state/journal is an engineering invalidity. No budget borrowing or retry.
+
+Runtime stays GPU7, frozen UUID/CUDA0/EGL4, current managed Codex CLI/chatgpt, gpt-6-astra/low/180s/E2; no Poe/fallback. Validate resolved owning worktree equality before permitting its frozen lexical compatibility alias. All runtime bytes/links, exact provider settings, source, task inputs, study private locks and GPU inventory remain enforced. Only N30 may use its exact variant-owned artifacts subdirectory below the old global runtime artifact root. Other cohort routes retain their original behavior.
+
+## Exact root activation order (not executed by CPU executor)
+
+1. Review final clean commit/source manifest, reverse records, CPU evidence, exact three composed profiles. Under idle study locks, integrate the reviewed commit into owning W; keep old artifacts. No data migration.
+2. From W with scripts available on sys.path, build source=w.source_record(W,c.source_paths(vars(r))), runtime=c.runtime_ref(), bridge=qd_ed_n30_bridge.build(source,runtime,W). Write bridge once to V/source-equivalence-bridge-v1.json. Do not run old proofs. Independently verify current source, frozen runtime, provider/login and exact GPU identity/boot/driver/occupancy.
+3. Write immutable V/final-source-runtime-review-v1.json with exactly c.final_review's expected fields: schema=n30-source-runtime-review-v1, disposition=accepted, source, runtime, protocol, source_plan, source_bridge, predecessor, budget_reuse, new_tensor_preflight=false, no_gpu_release=true. Root review itself is not release.
+4. Write V/adoption-v1/authority.json with exactly c.authority's fields: schema=n30-dev-authority-v1, cohort_id, source, runtime, protocol, final_review, budget_reuse, limits=c.LIMITS, local_gpu_hours=6.0, recorded_at, authority_interpretation, predecessor, validation_authorized=false, formal_authorized=false. Under existing private state locks, root adopts only state.n30_dev_authority={path,sha256}, retaining unchanged existing finite budget fields/ledger.
+5. Execute `python scripts/qd_ed_n30_prepare.py --output V/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json --freeze` from W. It creates exactly12 rows after whole source/runtime/admission checks; immutable existing plan is rejected. Independently check all12 full build_command/Hydra argv and future-QD-off exclusion. No model evaluation is needed for composition.
+6. Root writes V/execution-release-v1.json with exactly release_check fields: schema=n30-dev-execution-release-v1, plan ref, source_commit, cohort_id, ordered episode_keys, authority ref, physical_gpu7, limits, validation_authorized=false, formal_authorized=false. Fresh resource admission is required; earlier observations are not a substitute.
+7. Launch once from W: `python scripts/qd_ed_n30_supervise.py --plan V/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json --release V/execution-release-v1.json --status V/execution/supervisor-status-v1.json`. Replace V with its absolute path. Launch creates execution/ before supervisor.lock. Root records controller process identity/exit independently. No restart on failure.
+8. Terminal outputs are V/result-v1.json and execution/terminal-ledger-v1.json plus status. Root independently reviews costs, source, receipts and owned-process cleanup before any separate next phase. A valid terminal journal followed by status failure retains the journal accepted prefix/costs and forces INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED; it cannot silently promote or resume.
+
+External draft wrappers have executable=false and unresolved root refs. Unwrap/complete only after actual root review; the wrappers are intentionally rejected as authority/release documents. Their hashes are not embedded in source, preventing circular source/review/proof freezes.
