+# N30 Phase B: CPU execution integration
+
+Root has accepted scientific CPU commit `9029b384a34343efd73b4ea02184d83c5e52de61` in `root-phase-a-cpu-review-v1.json`. Continue in the same N30 implementation worktree from that commit. This is authorization for operational code, independent native-evidence auditing, mock tests, and draft documents only. No GPU, real checkpoint, simulator, API/network request, protected split, study state/ledger mutation, frozen production plan, or execution authority may be created by the executor.
+
+The scientific method is frozen by hypothesis-and-protocol-v1.md, the compute interpretation and root-trace-binding-clarification-v1.json. Keep that method and all default-off behavior unchanged. If actual integration exposes a necessary production instrumentation correction, describe the concrete issue to root before broadening the scientific delta. Reuse tested process/source/accounting helpers without refactoring unrelated cohorts.
+
+Implement the requirements in native-integration-requirements-draft-v1.md as the explicit N30 cohort path. Add an exact twelve-cell prospective Dev controller: original tasks0,1,2,3, each C0/Q0/N30 in that order, original frozen Dev task/init/env/policy identities, no inheritance/retry/resume of valid cells. C0 consumes baseline4; Q0/N30 consume development8. Candidate screen passes only after all four matched task blocks with at least3 successes and at least both control counts, plus substantive QD/ED/continuation and complete valid telemetry. At a complete three-arm block, stop numeric futility when candidate successes plus remaining tasks is below3. Unrun cells are Unknown. Validation/formal remain unauthorized; no screen outcome automatically dispatches them.
+
+Use current cumulative578 attempts/100 GPU hours and unchanged bucket caps76/262/180/40/20, retaining all prior charges, failures, and validation32/formal12 GPU-hour reservations. N30 has a6 GPU-hour local limit inclusive of preparation/proof/attempt/API-wait/audit/exit failures, with enough capacity reserved for a whole1800-second attempt plus40-second cleanup before dispatch. It may end RESOURCE_BUDGET_INCOMPLETE if a whole attempt no longer fits. This CPU release neither adopts the pending week proposal nor authorizes more spending.
+
+Bind final source, exact composed C0/Q0/N30 profiles, runtime, current managed Codex Stage login, provider, study-only locks/ledgers, and one admitted GPU worker. Preferred runtime is the already frozen GPU7 UUID/CUDA0/EGL4 mapping; boot/driver/occupancy must be revalidated by root at release. Keep the existing runtime/accounting framework and stop on invalid or incomplete evidence. Read operational reference metadata without modifying it. The final production source adoption, budget/source authority, plan freeze and launch belong to root.
+
+Extend the existing metered worker and receipt checks with the N30 path. Its independent audit uses the already captured native tensors: all8 actual action/EEF acknowledgments; prior native winner, unchanged decoder and committed prefix; original Main float64 target snapshot and strict distance comparison; immediate next-decision episode/reset/Stage/provider/target/tracker validity; source fresh population, shifted56+fresh8 row15, action mask, unchanged other15 rows, and canonical initial-row binding. Reconstruct from the actual native observations and existing generic execution events, not by trusting scalar claims or calling the online eligibility helper. Reject missing, stale, conflicting or contradictory evidence. Ordinary inactive reasons are distinct from malformed evidence. Verify terminal/reset/guidance-gap handling and nonactivation for C0/Q0. A continuation need not survive selection; never call an unchosen candidate a physical outcome.
+
+The new arithmetic is native copy/mask plus CPU float64 feedback, so source review, CPU tests and independent checks of actual recorded native tensors are appropriate. Do not add N29's unrelated standalone CUDA RBF arithmetic proof. Perform any production evidence audit inside the same metered worker; supervisor verifies bound receipts/hashes and scalar summaries without rerunning the tensor audit. Check actual total256 provider evaluations/16 score batches,19RBF,21B16 forwards per guided against unchanged Q0, separately from primary176/11 and5B1 forwards per unguided; whole-episode counts may vary. Check the explicit N30 initial_final diagnostic binding without adding a score batch.
+
+Store large future artifacts only through this variant's established artifacts symlink. Keep all CPU test logs, failures, manifests and draft outputs under this variant; no writes in other studies. Budget for this Phase B is600 process CPU seconds and2 threads with CUDA hidden, including test reruns; no installations or subdelegation. Use synthetic recorders/observations and source/config/plan fixtures, no existing experiment tensor load or hidden evaluator information. Meaningful tests must fail for changed identities/source/limits, stale or forged continuation evidence, incorrect actual/canonical row associations, extra scoring, post-futility dispatch and invalid promotion. Preserve failed tests; after required checks pass, stop repeating them absent a new change or concern.
+
+Deliver one clean commit (or documented sequence), exact source/patch references, minimal contract/native audit tests and resource logs, a draft plan/composition review, and a concise report explaining remaining root adoption/release steps. Do not change the scientific goal or claim CPU tests/native mechanics establish task success.
